// F186 (stage 8 step 1): when a call matches no member of an overload set and the members differ
// at the position that rejected it, the error names the *types that position accepts* rather than
// listing signatures. This is the shape the hand-written builtin arms use -- `len`'s says "expects
// an array, string, map, set, builder or Mutable" -- derived from the declarations instead of
// kept by hand, which is what converting those arms would need.
//
// The four builder types collapse to one phrase only when something else is there to contrast
// with; a set of builders alone would otherwise read "expects a builder", restating the question.
fn main() {
    print(fold(Set<int> { 1, 2 }, 0, fn(acc: int, x: int) -> int { return acc + x }))
}
